course: dictionary
lesson: 12637
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Dispatched is one of those words. «The shop dispatched my parcel this morning» means sent off, because a parcel is sent somewhere. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning.
explain: The same word can mean dealt with quickly. «Mia dispatched her maths homework in ten minutes» does not mean she sent it anywhere. It means she finished it fast. Ask yourself: what is being dispatched, and what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Sometimes a word is used to soften a hard truth. In hunting, farming, crime stories and history books, dispatched can mean killed quickly. «The hunter dispatched the rabbit at once, so it felt no pain.» This is a cool, technical word. It is not a word you need to use yourself, but you will meet it, so you must recognise it.
fact: Dispatched means sent off, dealt with quickly, or, in some books, killed quickly.
fact: Dispatch is the same word as despatch, which is the UK spelling.
fact: «Dispatched» means sent off when it is about a parcel, a message or a person.
fact: «Dispatched» means dealt with quickly when it is about a job or task.
fact: A euphemism is a softer or politer word used instead of a harder one, so the killing sense of dispatched is a euphemism.
exercise: «The shop dispatched my parcel this morning.» What does dispatched mean here? | Opened and emptied | Counted carefully | Lost forever | *Sent off
exercise: «The hunter dispatched the rabbit quickly, so it did not suffer.» What does dispatched mean here? | *Killed quickly | Washed and dried | Hid from sight | Fed carefully
exercise: «Mia dispatched her maths homework in ten minutes.» What does dispatched mean here? | Spilled on the floor | Eaten up slowly | *Dealt with quickly | Handed back to the teacher unfinished
test: Which spelling of dispatch is used in the UK as well? | Dispatchment | Dispose | Disperse | *Despatch
test: The courier «dispatched the package this afternoon.» What does this mean? | Sold in a shop | Stolen | Opened | *Sent off
exam: Which sentence uses dispatched to mean killed quickly? | «The post van dispatched at noon.» | *«The hunter dispatched the rabbit at once, so it felt no pain.» | «She dispatched a message to her friend.» | «The job was dispatched by lunch.»
